MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_001: Hmmm...
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_002: Uh... Something wrong, Tialla? You're staring at\nmy face.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_003: You're a bit different from the rest of us, Cai. You're\nthe child of a goddess.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_004: I always thought you had a mysterious grace about\nyou. You're not like the other kids in our village.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_005: I started wondering about where that difference\ncomes from. I guess I got a little lost in thought.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_006: Maybe I am different. But you're different than the\nother kids too.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_007: You lived in a big city before coming to our\nvillage, right?
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_008: Yes. But, well...Ribeira is Grandpa's hometown.\nHe moved back after...
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_009: Anyway, Grandpa was an amazing tactician. He\nloved books and collected a ton of them.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_010: One time, he stacked some books so high, the\nfloorboards underneath them gave out.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_011: Oh, wow. Heh, I don't think I've got it in me to finish\neven one book.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_012: It's easy if you put your mind to it. And books are so\ninteresting! You can learn so many things by reading.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_013: I'm impressed by how smart you are. Your grandpa\nmust be really proud.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_014: He passed his love of reading to you.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_015: Actually... Grandpa doesn't approve of my reading.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_016: He scolds me about it. It's scary!
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_017: But he should be happy that you're studying!
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_018: Right! You'd think so, wouldn't you?
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_019: But I have to read in secret, so he won't find out.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_020: I've read every book in the house.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_021: What?! All of them?! You just said one stack of 'em\nbroke the floor!
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_022: They're just so fascinating! I couldn't stop once\nI started!
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_023: The more knowledge you get, the more connections\nyou make in your head. The fun of it keeps growing!
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_024: Uh-huh. Just like I thought, Tialla. Between the two\nof us, you're the one who's different.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_025: I just can't imagine all those letters and words could\nbe that interesting.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_C_026: But I do wonder why your grandpa doesn't want\nyou reading... Hmm...
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_001: Hyah... Hah!
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_002: Looking good today, Cai. Doing some spear work?
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_003: Yup! Pop always says, "Drill with a spear every day!"
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_004: He says that a lot. He says the point is to learn to\nhandle a spear like it's an extension of your body.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_005: You've been practicing for a long time now, so it's\nprobably become a habit, right?
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_006: Yeah, you know how it works. Keep piling on\nthe training!
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_007: Even minimal gains can mean the difference\nbetween life and death on the battlefield.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_008: Right... You never know what's coming, I guess.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_009: So... Cai... Um...
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_010: Do you have any dreams for the future? Ideas for\nwhat you want to do, or be, or see?
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_011: Hm? Uh... I haven't really thought about it much.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_012: Really?
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_013: I would like to live with my dad and mom as a\nnormal family.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_014: Hearing Ultand talk about it had an impact, I guess.\nSeems like a family situation would be nice.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_015: Everything's up in the air right now though, so it's\nhard to predict how things will land.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_016: And I thought my mom was dead, but I got to meet\nher. So I do have a lot of questions for her.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_017: What about you, Tialla?
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_018: Me? Well... I have two dreams, I guess.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_019: First, I'd like to work at a temple and spend my free\ntime reading every book in their enormous library.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_020: I hear temple libraries are incredible! I bet I could\nread for the rest of my life and not get to every book.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_021: Hahaha. I bet that'd be a real happy place for\nyou, Tialla.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_022: But wouldn't your grandpa object? It'd mean you\nwouldn't come back to Ribeira, right?
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_023: Grandpa was actually very encouraging when I was\nleaving the village.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_024: He said, "Unless it's a decision you make for yourself,\nwherever you head off to, you'll regret it."
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_025: Wise words. Just what I'd expect from your grandpa.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_026: You're very clever, Tialla. I'm sure you'll find a way\nto make that dream come true.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_027: Hehe. I hope so.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_028: OK, so what's your other dream?
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_029: Oh... Um... That one's...a secret.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_030: What? That's mean! You told me half of the story.\nWhat's the rest?
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_031: Well... This is a dream that I can't fulfill by myself.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_032: What's with the riddles? Just tell me!
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_033: Oh! Time's up! We're done talking about this.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_034: Hey! That wasn't long enough! It's like you don't\neven want me to guess!
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_035: Back to your training. I'll watch from the sidelines.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_036: Fine. Whatever.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_037: Definitely a dream that I can't fulfill by myself.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_038: It can't come true...without you.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_039: But I'll be an old lady before Cai shows any real\nsigns of age.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_B_040: Cai... I wish we could be together forever.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_001: Whatcha readin' now, Tialla?
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_002: It's so cool! It has diagrams of plants from the\nancient era, and it even tells you how to grow them.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_003: Huh... A book with pictures. Even I might be able to\nget through that one.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_004: When you get your temple job, maybe you could let\nme know about any interesting books you find there.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_005: I hope I become a priest that everyone can rely on.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_006: Your dream is bound to come true. I'm rooting\nfor you!
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_007: Thank you. Cai, when all this fighting ends...
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_008: I guess you'll go back to Ribeira, won't you?\nTogether with your mom and dad?
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_009: Huh? I don't know if I'll go back to the village.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_010: You don't? Really?
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_011: Yeah, Mom and Pop aren't from there.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_012: Pop knew Peter's mom, and he turned to her for\nhelp. That's his only real connection to that place.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_013: Right...
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_014: And Mom's been stuck in her temple all this time, so\nI'd like to take her to see a lot of different places.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_015: I'm thinking we'll spend some time wandering all\naround Dagda.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_016: I wonder if Aurora gets lonely...since people she\nloved die long before her.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_017: I'm sure it bothers her, but she told me it isn't the\nlength of the relationship that matters.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_018: What matters is living life to the fullest with the ones\nyou cherish, while making irreplaceable memories.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_019: I see... Makes sense...
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_020: That's it!
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_021: What?! What're you talking about?
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_022: I figured it out! I can make both of my dreams work!
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_023: Cai, listen. I'll tell you about my other dream, the\none I couldn't share with you before.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_024: My dream is...to be together with you...forever!
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_025: I was afraid of how I'd grow old long before you did.\nAnd I couldn't figure out a solution to that.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_026: But hearing you talk about your mother—hearing her\nthoughts about time and love—I made up my mind.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_027: Cai! I want us to be together until I die!
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_035: Uh... Tialla... Are you saying...
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_028: Have your adventures around Dagda. Just make sure\nyou come back for me.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_029: We won't have to worry about making a living.\nMy temple job will provide for us.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_030: And not just us! Your mother and father too! I can\nsupport all of us!
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_031: Tialla...this makes me so happy. But I hope you can\nbe content with someone like me.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_032: So much about the life ahead of me is unclear...
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_033: But whatever comes, I will cherish you for all time\nand protect you always.
MID_SE_Kai_Tia_A_034: The love my mom and dad have for each other will\nbe our guide.